  "name": "Isleño décimas (St. Bernard Parish Canary Islander ballads)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Sung Spanish narrative poems of the Isleños, descendants of Canary Islanders settled by the Spanish colonial government in St. Bernard Parish, Louisiana, in the late 18th century, whose trapping and fishing communities centred on Delacroix Island. Décimas recount local events, storms, hunting and courtship alongside older Spanish romances, sung unaccompanied by a solo singer in a free, declamatory style; Irván Pérez, named an NEA National Heritage Fellow in 1991, was its best-known singer and composer, and Samuel G. Armistead documented the repertoire.",
